From: aps3e-s26 <aps3e-s26@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:53:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/10] rsx: sleep instead of spinning once the FIFO has idled

With the FIFO empty or parked on a jump-to-self, the RSX thread yields in
a loop. On Android the yield returns immediately when nothing else is
runnable on that core, so RSX keeps a prime core at 100% while the game
waits on the PPU. The Odin 3 fork measured the stock build at 104-105 C
with the RSX thread at 97% (Snapdragon 8 Elite). On a phone that heat is
taken back from the PPU/SPU threads through throttling.

After the FIFO has been idle for one slice, sleep in slices (default
100 us, new "Video|RSX Idle Sleep" setting, 0 restores spinning) and run
the local tasks right after each sleep so flips, interrupts and flush
requests are not left to every 64th iteration.

Based on HamzaDevz/aps3e 719f52bba (odin3 branch).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QHcVVDuR9mxorL6GkyZmzr
